  <Telescope>
    <aperture unit="cm">80</aperture>
    <description>             The Stratospheric TeraHertz Observatory (STO) telescope is a light-weight telescope designed to be carried as part of a balloon-borne payload.  It has an 80cm diamater hyperboloid primary mirror designed for maximum performance in the 300-5000nm wavelength range. This telescope originally flew on the Stratospheric TeraHertz Observatory and was refitted to be carried by the BOPPS (balloon observatory) gondola.         </description>
